// Change: new rule
// Title: Suspicious Shadow File Access via Standard Utilities
// Sigma ID: e996fae2-3045-4569-9dfe-c45c0c268c5c
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: David Akanno (@davidakanno56-bit)
// Date: 2026-10-05 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: credential_access, T1003.008
// Description: Detects standard text and file inspection utilities accessing shadow files to extract password
//   hashes or inspect local credentials.
// False positives:
//   - Administrative user audit scripts
//   - Backup utilities running under authorized service accounts
// References:
//   - https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1003/008/
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/0b5491472ea42005d50a52a34efaaab2cdb68d55/rules/linux/process_creation/proc_creation_lnx_susp_shadow_access.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language, Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where (ProcessCommandLine contains "/etc/shadow" or ProcessCommandLine contains "/etc/gshadow") and (FolderPath endswith "/cat" or FolderPath endswith "/head" or FolderPath endswith "/tail" or FolderPath endswith "/more" or FolderPath endswith "/less" or FolderPath endswith "/grep" or FolderPath endswith "/awk")
